S['52'] = dict(tag='syllabus',
simple="<span class='hl'>Lis pendens</span> (pending litigation): while a genuine court case about a right to immovable property is pending, <span class='hl'>no party can transfer or deal with that property so as to affect the other party's rights</span> under the final decree, unless the court permits. A buyer during the case takes subject to the result.",
deep="""<ol><li><b>Suit or proceeding pending</b> in a competent court in India (or one established beyond India by the Central Government).</li>
<li><b>Not collusive:</b> a fake suit set up by the parties does not attract the rule.</li>
<li><b>Right to immovable property directly and specifically in question:</b> the suit must be about that property itself (title, possession, partition, mortgage), not merely a money claim.</li>
<li><b>Transfer or dealing by a party:</b> sale, mortgage, lease, gift, even court sales in execution.</li>
<li><b>Effect:</b> the transfer is not void, but it cannot affect the rights of the other party under the decree. The transferee is bound by the result, whether or not he knew of the case. Good faith is irrelevant: the doctrine rests on public policy, not notice.</li>
<li><b>Exception:</b> transfer with the court's authority and on its terms.</li>
<li><b>Explanation (period):</b> pendency starts on presentation of the plaint or institution of the proceeding in a competent court, and continues until final decree or order and complete satisfaction or discharge, or until execution becomes time-barred.</li>
<li><b>Purpose:</b> otherwise a party could defeat any suit by transferring the property, and litigation would never end.</li></ol>""",
dissect=[("During the pendency in any Court","Suit must be pending."),("which is not collusive","Genuine dispute."),("any right to immoveable property is directly and specifically in question","Property itself in issue."),("cannot be transferred or otherwise dealt with by any party to the suit or proceeding","Bar on parties."),("so as to affect the rights of any other party thereto under any decree or order","Transfer not void, but subject to decree."),("except under the authority of the Court and on such terms as it may impose","Court's permission."),("from the date of the presentation of the plaint or the institution of the proceeding","Start."),("complete satisfaction or discharge of such decree or order has been obtained, or has become unobtainable","End.")],
master=dict(story="On 1 January 2026 Meera files a partition suit against Arjun for half of the family farm. On 1 March Arjun sells the whole farm to Kabir, who checks the land records but does not search court records and has no idea of the suit. On 1 April Arjun mortgages another plot to a bank; that plot is not in the suit. On 1 May Arjun, with the court's permission, sells a strip to pay court-ordered maintenance. Separately, Suresh and Ramesh file a fake suit between themselves to block a third party's purchase. In December 2027 the court decrees half the farm to Meera; the decree is executed in 2028.",steps=[("Kabir's purchase?","Valid between Arjun and Kabir, but subject to Meera's decree: Meera gets her half; Kabir keeps only Arjun's half. His good faith does not help."),("Bank mortgage of the other plot?","Not affected: that plot was not directly in question."),("Court-permitted sale?","Valid on the court's terms."),("Suresh and Ramesh's suit?","Collusive: no lis pendens."),("When did pendency end?","On complete satisfaction of the decree in 2028.")]),
ills=[("Sale during suit","Defendant sells the suit property mid-case.","m","Buyer bound by the decree","s.52."),("Good faith buyer","Buyer had no notice of the suit.","m","Still bound","Public policy, not notice."),("Money suit","Suit only for recovery of a loan; debtor sells his house.","y","Not affected","No right to immovable property directly in question."),("Collusive suit","Parties stage a fake case.","y","No lis pendens","Not collusive requirement."),("Court permission","Sale with the court's leave.","y","Valid on terms","Exception."),("After satisfaction","Sale after the decree is fully executed.","y","Not affected","Pendency ended.")],
exam=dict(q="Explain the doctrine of lis pendens. (10 marks)",pts=["Meaning and object","Essentials: pending suit, competent court, not collusive, property directly in question, transfer by a party","Effect: not void, but subject to the decree; notice irrelevant","Court's permission","Period under the Explanation"],line="Under s.52, during the pendency of a non-collusive suit in which a right to immovable property is directly and specifically in question, the property cannot be transferred by a party so as to affect another party's rights under the decree, except with the court's authority."),
quiz=[("A buyer during a pending title suit who had no notice of it:",["Takes free","Is bound by the decree","Gets priority"],1,"Notice is irrelevant."),("Does lis pendens apply to a pure money suit?",["Yes","No","Only after decree"],1,"Property must be directly in question.")],
links=[("CPC Order 39","Injunctions during suits."),("s.3","Notice (not the basis of s.52)."),("s.53","Fraudulent transfers.")],
next="Section 53 strikes at transfers made to cheat creditors or later buyers.")

S['53'] = dict(tag='syllabus',
simple="A transfer of immovable property made <span class='hl'>to defeat or delay creditors</span> can be cancelled at the option of any creditor so affected (but an honest buyer for value is protected). And a <span class='hl'>free transfer made to cheat a later buyer</span> can be cancelled by that later buyer.",
deep="""<ol><li><b>Sub-section (1), creditors:</b> a transfer with intent to defeat or delay the transferor's creditors is <i>voidable</i> at the option of any creditor so defeated or delayed.
<ul><li>Protection: rights of a transferee in good faith and for consideration are not impaired.</li>
<li>Insolvency law is not affected.</li>
<li>The creditor's suit (\"creditor\" includes a decree-holder) must be brought on behalf of, or for the benefit of, <b>all</b> the creditors.</li>
<li>Paying or securing one genuine creditor in preference to others is not, by itself, a fraudulent transfer.</li></ul></li>
<li><b>Sub-section (2), later transferees:</b> a transfer <b>without consideration</b> made with intent to defraud a later transferee is voidable at that later transferee's option. But a gift is not presumed fraudulent merely because a later transfer for value was made.</li>
<li><b>Voidable, not void:</b> valid until the affected person chooses to set it aside.</li>
<li><b>Intent</b> is judged from the circumstances (relationship of parties, inadequate price, secrecy, retaining possession, timing just before a decree).</li></ol>""",
dissect=[("with intent to defeat or delay the creditors of the transferor","Intent to cheat creditors."),("shall be voidable at the option of any creditor so defeated or delayed","Voidable at creditor's option."),("shall impair the rights of a transferee in good faith and for consideration","Honest buyer protected."),("shall be instituted on behalf of, or for the benefit of, all the creditors","Representative suit."),("made without consideration with intent to defraud a subsequent transferee","Sub-section (2)."),("no transfer made without consideration shall be deemed to have been made with intent to defraud by reason only that a subsequent transfer for consideration was made","No automatic presumption.")],
master=dict(story="Arjun owes ₹40 lakh to four creditors. Days before a decree in Ramesh's suit, Arjun gifts his house to his wife and keeps living in it. He also \"sells\" his shop to his friend for ₹1 lakh (worth ₹30 lakh), cash never actually paid. He sells his farm at full market price to Kabir, who knows nothing of the debts. He pays his genuine creditor, the bank, in full by transferring a plot to it. Separately, Raghunath gifts a plot to Meera, then sells the same plot to Suresh for value; Raghunath had planned the gift to cheat Suresh.",steps=[("Gift to wife?","Voidable at the creditors' option: intent to defeat them (timing, family, continued possession)."),("Sham sale to the friend?","Voidable: no real consideration and fraudulent intent."),("Sale to Kabir?","Protected: good faith and consideration."),("Plot to the bank?","Preferring one genuine creditor is not by itself fraudulent."),("How must Ramesh sue?","On behalf of or for the benefit of all creditors."),("Suresh vs Meera's gift?","Voidable at Suresh's option under (2): gratuitous transfer intended to defraud him (fraud must be proved; the later sale alone does not prove it).")]),
ills=[("Gift to dodge creditors","Debtor gifts property to a relative just before decree.","n","Voidable","s.53(1)."),("Honest buyer","Buyer for value without knowledge of fraud.","y","Protected","Good faith and consideration."),("Preference","Debtor pays one creditor with property.","y","Not fraudulent by itself","Preference allowed."),("Later buyer","Gift made to defeat a later purchaser.","n","Voidable by him","s.53(2)."),("No presumption","Gift followed later by a sale, no evidence of fraud.","y","Gift stands","Explanation to (2).")],
exam=dict(q="Explain fraudulent transfer under s.53. (10 marks)",pts=["Sub-section (1): intent to defeat or delay creditors; voidable","Protection of bona fide purchaser for value; insolvency law saved","Representative suit for all creditors; preference not fraud","Sub-section (2): gratuitous transfer to defraud later transferee; no presumption","Badges of fraud"],line="Under s.53, a transfer of immovable property made with intent to defeat or delay creditors is voidable at the option of any creditor so affected, and a gratuitous transfer to defraud a subsequent transferee is voidable at his option."),
quiz=[("A fraudulent transfer under s.53 is:",["Void","Voidable","Valid"],1,"Voidable at the option of the person defrauded."),("A buyer for value in good faith from a fraudulent debtor:",["Loses the property","Is protected","Must pay twice"],1,"Protection clause.")],
links=[("Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code, 2016","Avoidance of preferential and undervalued transactions (insolvency law saved)."),("s.52","Lis pendens.")],
next="Section 53A protects a buyer in possession under a written contract.")

S['53A'] = dict(tag='syllabus',
simple="<span class='hl'>Part performance</span>: if you agree in writing to buy property, take <span class='hl'>possession</span> under that agreement, and are ready to do your part, the seller <span class='hl'>cannot throw you out</span> just because the formal sale deed was never completed. It is a <span class='hl'>shield, not a sword</span>.",
deep="""<ol><li><b>A contract to transfer immovable property for consideration.</b></li>
<li><b>In writing, signed</b> by the transferor or on his behalf, from which the terms can be ascertained with reasonable certainty.</li>
<li><b>Possession:</b> the transferee has taken possession of the property or part of it in part performance, or, already being in possession, continues in possession in part performance and has done some act in furtherance of the contract.</li>
<li><b>Readiness:</b> the transferee has performed or is willing to perform his part.</li>
<li><b>Effect:</b> where the transfer has not been completed in the manner prescribed by law, the transferor (and anyone claiming under him) is barred from enforcing against the transferee any right in respect of the property in his possession, other than a right expressly provided by the contract.</li>
<li><b>Proviso:</b> a later transferee for consideration without notice of the contract or its part performance is not affected.</li>
<li><b>Shield, not sword:</b> it gives a defence to protect possession; it does not give title or a cause of action to sue for ownership.</li>
<li><b>Limitation:</b> the defence remains available even if a suit for specific performance has become time-barred, provided the conditions are met.</li>
<li><b>2001 amendment:</b> the words \"the contract, though required to be registered, has not been registered, or\" were removed, and the Registration Act s.17(1A) and s.49 now require such agreements made after 2001 to be registered; an unregistered one cannot be used for s.53A protection.</li></ol>""",
dissect=[("contracts to transfer for consideration any immoveable property by writing signed by him or on his behalf","Written, signed contract."),("the terms necessary to constitute the transfer can be ascertained with reasonable certainty","Certain terms."),("in part performance of the contract, taken possession of the property or any part thereof","Possession taken."),("being already in possession, continues in possession in part performance of the contract and has done some act in furtherance","Possession continued plus an act."),("has performed or is willing to perform his part of the contract","Readiness."),("the transfer has not been completed in the manner prescribed therefor by the law","Formalities incomplete."),("shall be debarred from enforcing against the transferee","Shield against the transferor."),("other than a right expressly provided by the terms of the contract","Contract rights preserved."),("who has no notice of the contract or of the part performance thereof","Proviso: bona fide later purchaser.")],
master=dict(story="In 2024 Raghunath signs a registered and stamped written agreement to sell his orchard to Kabir for ₹40 lakh, terms fully stated; Kabir pays ₹30 lakh and is put in possession; the balance is due on execution of the sale deed. Kabir repeatedly offers the balance, but Raghunath refuses to sign the deed. In 2028 Raghunath sues to evict Kabir. Kabir never sued for specific performance and that suit is now time-barred. Meanwhile, in 2027 Raghunath sold the orchard to Suresh, who inspected the orchard and saw Kabir's workers harvesting. Separately, Ramesh occupies Raghunath's shop under only an oral agreement to buy it. A third buyer, Das, holds an unregistered 2025 written agreement and possession. And Ramesh's tenant-turned-buyer friend, already in possession as tenant, signs a registered written agreement to buy and then pays the price, but does nothing else.",steps=[("Can Raghunath evict Kabir?","No: written signed contract with certain terms, possession taken in part performance, readiness shown, deed not completed. s.53A shields Kabir."),("Does it matter that Kabir's specific performance suit is time-barred?","No: the defence is still available."),("Does Kabir become owner?","No: s.53A is a shield, not a sword; title still needs a registered sale deed."),("Suresh?","Not protected by the proviso: Kabir's possession gave him notice. Suresh cannot evict Kabir."),("Ramesh (oral agreement)?","No protection: the contract must be in writing."),("Das (unregistered 2025 agreement)?","No protection: after 2001 the agreement must be registered (Registration Act s.17(1A), s.49)."),("The tenant who paid the price?","Continuing possession plus an act in furtherance of the contract (payment) qualifies.")]),
ills=[("Classic shield","Buyer in possession under a written signed contract, ready to pay.","y","Cannot be evicted","s.53A."),("Oral contract","Possession under an oral agreement.","n","No protection","Writing required."),("No possession","Written agreement, price paid, but no possession.","n","No protection","Possession is essential."),("Unwilling buyer","Buyer refuses to pay the balance.","n","No protection","Readiness required."),("Bona fide later buyer","Later purchaser for value with no notice (buyer not in visible possession).","n","Proviso protects the later buyer","Proviso."),("Sword","Buyer sues to be declared owner under s.53A.","n","Not available","Shield only.")],
exam=dict(q="Explain the doctrine of part performance. (10 marks)",pts=["Object: protect a transferee in possession","Essentials: written signed contract, certain terms, possession, act, readiness","Effect: transferor debarred; shield not sword","Proviso: bona fide purchaser without notice","Limitation does not bar the defence; 2001 amendment and Registration Act s.17(1A), s.49"],line="Under s.53A, where a transferee under a written signed contract to transfer immovable property has taken possession in part performance and is willing to perform, the transferor is debarred from enforcing rights against him, though the transfer is not completed as required by law."),
quiz=[("s.53A gives the buyer:",["Title","A shield to protect possession","A right to sue for damages only"],1,"Shield, not sword."),("Is an oral agreement enough?",["Yes","No","Only for small plots"],1,"Writing signed by the transferor is required.")],
links=[("s.54","A contract for sale creates no interest."),("Registration Act s.17(1A), s.49","Registration of part performance agreements after 2001."),("Specific Relief Act, 1963","Specific performance.")],
next="Chapter III begins: Section 54 defines sale.")
